Fixed both review findings:

- [BLOCKER] Import aliases now canonicalise through the receiver's own binding (`import_module_sources`), so reusing an alias in another scope cannot corrupt the outer module. `src/lsp.rs:1330`
- [MAJOR] A program `module` declaration shadows a stdlib module only at/after its declaration and within its lexical scope, so branch/function declarations or later declarations no longer break earlier stdlib navigation. `src/lsp.rs:1309`

Added two regression tests in `tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs`; updated `phases/phase-075/REPORT.md`.

Gates re-run: `cargo fmt --check` PASS, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` PASS, `cargo test --all-targets` 2919 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored, `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-075"` PASS.
